WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.720
South Africa's Central Bank raised its repo rate by a quarter point to 7.25% pushing up

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:12.920
loan costs for borrowers. This is Omni View Africa &amp; Middle East, episode 2. I'm Mira,

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:18.000
the Nerra Network's AI host. The Monetary Policy Committee of the South African Reserve

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:25.880
Bank voted unanimously to raise the repo rate by 25 basis points from 7% to 7.25%.

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:32.360
The prime lending rate rose automatically from 10.5% to 10.75%.

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:37.820
Headline inflation reached 4.4% in August, while the central bank projects it will peak

00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:39.860
at 5.7% in November.

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:43.600
Services inflation stood at 5.1% in August.

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:48.640
The economy contracted 0.2% in the second quarter of 2026.

00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:54.300
Prompting the bank to lower its full-year GDP growth forecast to 1.2%.

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:59.580
Market analysts viewed the move as a preventive step to anchor expectations rather than the

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:01.300
start of a longer tightening cycle.

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:07.760
Chief economist Johann Ells at PSG Financial Services noted the unanimous vote was more

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:08.900
hawkish than expected.

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:14.980
Supplyside price shocks are initially inflationary, but ultimately deflationary for demand and

00:01:14.980 --> 00:01:16.400
growth, according to Ells.

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:21.120
The adjustment marks the second such increase since the government ended austerity measures.

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:26.120
The decision came the day before Heritage Day when many South Africans gather for

00:01:26.120 --> 00:01:30.800
Brise. Archbishop Desmond Tutu had earlier linked the day to Brise celebrations,

00:01:31.160 --> 00:01:36.180
which boosted retail sales. The bank cited elevated long-term inflation expectations

00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:39.400
above its 3 percent midpoint target as a key factor.

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:44.420
Across the region, the International Criminal Court convicted Central African Republic

00:01:44.420 --> 00:01:53.140
Select a rebel commander, Muhammad Sayyid Abdel-Khani, on four counts, including torture and persecution for acts during the 2013 conflict.

00:01:53.680 --> 00:02:03.560
Prosecutors said Sayyid ran a bang-wee prison, where suspected supporters of former president François Bozizei were beaten and held in a windowless cell beneath his office floorboards.

00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:11.100
Central African Republic Justice Minister Arno Dubai Abazin welcomed the ruling and said no victim will be left behind.

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:16.800
The 2013 seizure of power by predominantly Muslim seleka rebels triggered opposition

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:22.220
from mainly Christian anti-Balaka militias, detainees testified about beatings and harsh

00:02:22.220 --> 00:02:23.340
conditions in the prison.

00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:28.340
The conviction covers events from the height of the conflict that ousted President Bozize.

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:34.280
Sudan's paramilitary rapid support forces carried out drone attacks on government held towns

00:02:34.280 --> 00:02:35.660
in North Kortafan State.

00:02:35.660 --> 00:02:41.960
One strike hit a crowded courtroom in Umruwaba on September 8, and killed about 10 people while

00:02:41.960 --> 00:02:44.340
injuring dozens, according to emergency lawyers.

00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:49.620
A second strike the next day hit a college in Allo Bede, killing a security guard and

00:02:49.620 --> 00:02:50.840
damaging eight classrooms.

00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:54.440
The Dean of the College set the entire faculty felt destroyed.

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:59.400
A student who had taken exams the previous day described her future as destroyed.

00:03:00.080 --> 00:03:04.960
The United Nations reported that drone attacks by both sides killed more than 1,000 civilians

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:06.320
in the first half of the year.

00:03:06.860 --> 00:03:09.440
Residents describe the strikes as part of a new campaign

00:03:09.870 --> 00:03:11.600
after weeks of reduced activity.

00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:14.820
The rapid support forces said it does not intentionally

00:03:14.820 --> 00:03:15.680
target civilians.

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:19.820
A hospital patient in Umarwaba who fled earlier bombardment

00:03:19.820 --> 00:03:22.680
distinguished between strategic and suicide drones.

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:26.820
Also today, new patriotic party communicator Dennis Miracles

00:03:26.820 --> 00:03:29.700
Abawagiye said Ghana's vessel traffic management

00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:32.820
information system has been out of operation at sites

00:03:32.820 --> 00:03:38.520
including Ado-Wineba, Axum, Keta, and Halfocene, forcing reliance on a less

00:03:38.520 --> 00:03:42.720
comprehensive skylight system. The communicator argued that the system cannot

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:46.420
provide continuous coverage for detecting smaller vessels outside port

00:03:46.420 --> 00:03:50.420
limits. He linked the surveillance gap to increased risks of narcotics

00:03:50.420 --> 00:03:54.680
movement through Ghana's maritime domain. The Ghana Maritime Authority rejected

00:03:54.680 --> 00:03:59.480
the claim and said its systems remain operational. Abawagiye maintained that

00:03:59.480 --> 00:04:03.920
the collapse of the Vessel Traffic Management Information System, removed a key detection

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:05.020
and interception layer.

00:04:05.660 --> 00:04:09.780
Nigeria and the United States signed a framework agreement for cooperation and geological

00:04:09.780 --> 00:04:13.260
data, mineral development, processing, and infrastructure.

00:04:13.700 --> 00:04:19.020
With Nigeria's Minister of Solid Minerals Development, Delhi Alakay stating the goal is to retain

00:04:19.020 --> 00:04:22.020
more value inside the country through local processing.

00:04:22.580 --> 00:04:27.480
The agreement was signed in New York by Alakay and US Deputy Secretary of State Christopher

00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:28.040
Landau.

00:04:28.040 --> 00:04:32.720
It covers the mineral value chain from exploration through development and processing.

00:04:33.520 --> 00:04:37.720
Alaka said Nigeria does not want to remain primarily an exporter of raw minerals.

00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:43.640
The pact identifies infrastructure as one area for cooperation that could stimulate demand for

00:04:43.640 --> 00:04:49.040
industrial property and logistics facilities near production areas. The wider world includes a

00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:54.660
plan by Djibouti, Ethiopia, and the Dango Tay Group for a petroleum pipeline that would link

00:04:54.660 --> 00:05:00.120
Ethiopian refineries to the port of Djibouti, according to Ethiopian Prime Minister Abbi Ahmed.

00:05:00.860 --> 00:05:06.100
The project aims to improve export routes for refined petroleum products. It would connect inland

00:05:06.100 --> 00:05:11.320
production sites to coastal facilities in Djibouti. The announcement came during regional economic

00:05:11.320 --> 00:05:17.060
discussions. The case on both sides involves Ghana's opposition and the Ghana Maritime Authority

00:05:17.060 --> 00:05:22.200
disagreeing on whether the vessel traffic management information system remains fully operational

00:05:22.200 --> 00:05:23.820
for monitoring the country's waters.

00:05:24.640 --> 00:05:27.300
Miracles Abuage of the New Patriotic Party

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:29.460
argues the system has been down for months

00:05:29.460 --> 00:05:30.960
at multiple coastal sites

00:05:30.960 --> 00:05:33.420
and that reliance on the skylight alternative

00:05:33.420 --> 00:05:35.460
leaves smaller vessels and activities

00:05:35.460 --> 00:05:37.300
outside port limits undetected,

00:05:37.820 --> 00:05:39.620
increasing risks of narcotics movement.

00:05:40.320 --> 00:05:41.940
The Ghana Maritime Authority states

00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:43.540
its systems remain operational

00:05:43.540 --> 00:05:46.520
for monitoring activities within Ghana's maritime space.

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:49.160
Both sides accept that continuous detection

00:05:49.160 --> 00:05:52.120
capability matters for intercepting illicit consignments.

00:05:52.580 --> 00:05:57.240
The next step is continued public statements from both the authority and opposition figures,

00:05:57.680 --> 00:05:59.280
without a scheduled resolution date.

00:05:59.920 --> 00:06:02.320
Abawage specifically named sites at Aata,

00:06:02.760 --> 00:06:06.520
Winneba, Axum, Keta, and Halfocene as affected.

00:06:06.980 --> 00:06:10.660
He said the CCTV cameras at those sites were also not functioning.

00:06:11.280 --> 00:06:15.700
The authority issued a statement on September 23 rejecting the claims of downtime.

00:06:15.700 --> 00:06:20.900
A sign of progress comes from the World Health Organization, which reported Ebola infection

00:06:20.900 --> 00:06:27.920
cases dropped by approximately 26% in ituri province and 15% in out ULA province over

00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:30.960
the last 21 days during the outbreak in DR Congo.

00:06:31.480 --> 00:06:36.260
Response efforts have been scaled up significantly more than 130 days into the outbreak.

00:06:36.960 --> 00:06:39.960
Health experts describe the first encouraging signs of progress.

00:06:39.960 --> 00:06:46.140
North Kivu Province, however, recorded a 73% increase in cases over the same period.

00:06:46.600 --> 00:06:49.160
That's OmniView Africa and Middle East for today.

